# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere.
#
# This is not cosmetic: the git hooks and .github/ci-run.sh are bash scripts.
# A CRLF checkout makes the shebang line `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which fails
# on Linux CI runners and in git-bash with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
# Forcing LF in the working tree too keeps Windows clones runnable.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the executable surface — never let a core.autocrlf setting win.
*.sh                         text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/pre-push   text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
*.yml                       text eol=lf
*.yaml                      text eol=lf
*.env                       text eol=lf

# Binaries — project-specific types (05 §2.3.3): self-hosted font files (05 §3.8.1) and WebP images.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.webp  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary

# Append-only shared record files: parallel task branches only add lines
# (newest entry at the top), so a union merge keeps both sides instead of
# conflicting. Do NOT add files whose lines are edited in place
# (IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md table cells, DEFERRED_BACKLOG.md header counter,
# CONTEXT.md). Note: GitHub's own mergeability check may ignore merge drivers;
# this helps local `git merge origin/main` on task branches.
Docs/STATUS_CHANGELOG.md merge=union
.claude/memory/MEMORY.md merge=union
